From bf7279ea181ca80715540e934742cce2318fca56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sukrit Jaidee <45908411+SukritJaAIproject@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:52:08 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] fix(desktop): research panel claims follow the grid on
 screen

Review findings on the v4 research grid, each reproduced first:

- "Projection-replay agreement 100%" is now a per-grid field. It was measured
  only for the 2026-09-12 set's SLAC replay; the v4 set was never replayed, so
  its tile reads "Not replayed for this model set".
- The panel subtitle mentions ISO 15118-2 results only when the grid has an
  ISO-2 arm; for v4 it says ISO 15118-2 is not yet measured.
- An unmeasured arm's reason was only a tooltip on a disabled tab, which
  keyboard and touch users never see. It is now a visible caption under the
  tabs, linked with aria-describedby.
- The Thai published-profile note now says the models were trained to flag
  those 369 sessions, as the English does.

Tests: 16 files / 294 pass; tsc adds no error.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
